$PQRS$ is a parallelogram with $PQ \parallel RS$ and $PS \parallel QR$. The diagonal $PR$ is drawn.
Which proof correctly establishes $\triangle PQR \cong \triangle RSP$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,decorations.markings}
\tikzset{sa/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{Stealth}}}}},da/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.4 with {\arrow{Stealth}},mark=at position 0.56 with {\arrow{Stealth}}}}}}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (4.2,0);
\coordinate (R) at (5.4,2.5);
\coordinate (S) at (1.2,2.5);
\draw[sa] (P)--(Q);
\draw[da] (Q)--(R);
\draw[sa] (S)--(R);
\draw[da] (P)--(S);
\draw (P)--(R);
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above right] at (R) {$R$};
\node[above left] at (S) {$S$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the proof that the diagonals of parallelogram $ABCD$ bisect each other at $E$, what is the reason that $\angle BAE = \angle DCE$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,decorations.markings,calc}
\tikzset{sa/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{Stealth}}}}},da/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.4 with {\arrow{Stealth}},mark=at position 0.56 with {\arrow{Stealth}}}}}}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (6,2.2);
\coordinate (D) at (1.4,2.2);
\draw[sa] (A)--(B);
\draw[da] (B)--(C);
\draw[sa] (D)--(C);
\draw[da] (A)--(D);
\coordinate (E) at (3,1.1);
\draw (A)--(C);
\draw (B)--(D);
\node[above left] at (3.15,1.25) {$E$};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above left] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\triangle ABC$ is isosceles with $AB = AC$ and $M$ is the midpoint of $BC$.
Which congruence test proves $\triangle ABM \cong \triangle ACM$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,decorations.markings,calc}
\tikzset{tk/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}},tk2/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (-2pt,-4pt)--(-2pt,4pt);\draw (2pt,-4pt)--(2pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (A) at (2.2,3.4);
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (M) at (2.2,0);
\draw[tk2] (A)--(B);
\draw[tk2] (A)--(C);
\draw[tk] (B)--(M);
\draw[tk] (M)--(C);
\draw (A)--(M);

\node[above] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (M) {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

