To prove the diagonals of square $ABCD$ are equal, $\triangle ABC$ and $\triangle DCB$ are compared.
Which congruence test is used?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,decorations.markings,calc}
\tikzset{tk/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.4,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3.4,3.4);
\coordinate (D) at (0,3.4);
\draw[tk] (A)--(B);
\draw[tk] (B)--(C);
\draw[tk] (C)--(D);
\draw[tk] (D)--(A);
\coordinate (sap) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\coordinate (saq) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(D)$);
\draw (sap)--($(sap)+(saq)-(A)$)--(saq);
\coordinate (sbp) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\coordinate (sbq) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\draw (sbp)--($(sbp)+(sbq)-(B)$)--(sbq);
\coordinate (scp) at ($(C)!0.3cm!(D)$);
\coordinate (scq) at ($(C)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\draw (scp)--($(scp)+(scq)-(C)$)--(scq);
\coordinate (sdp) at ($(D)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (sdq) at ($(D)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (sdp)--($(sdp)+(sdq)-(D)$)--(sdq);
\coordinate (E) at (1.7,1.7);
\draw (A)--(C);
\draw (B)--(D);
\node[above left] at (1.82,1.82) {$E$};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above left] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$PQRS$ is a kite with $PQ = PS$ and $RQ = RS$. The diagonal $PR$ is drawn.
