In isosceles $\triangle ABC$ ($AB = AC$), the line $AM$ bisects the apex angle $\angle BAC$.
Which congruence test proves $\triangle ABM \cong \triangle ACM$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,decorations.markings}
\tikzset{tk2/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (-2pt,-4pt)--(-2pt,4pt);\draw (2pt,-4pt)--(2pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (A) at (2.2,3.4);
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (M) at (2.2,0);
\draw[tk2] (A)--(B);
\draw[tk2] (A)--(C);
\draw (B)--(C);
\draw (A)--(M);
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.7cm]{angle=B--A--M};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.7cm]{angle=M--A--C};
